-# Render / Next.js 16 build fixes — 2026-09-03
-
-This revision addresses the concrete errors shown by the Render Docker build.
-
-## Build command
-
-- Production uses `next build --webpack` for Next.js 16 compatibility.
-- Docker build stage sets `CI=1`.
-
-## TypeScript sign-in fix
-
-The repository contained three role-specific sign-in pages that pass role information to the shared `AuthForm`, while the shared component previously accepted only `returnTo`.
-
-`AuthForm` now accepts:
-
-- `returnTo`
-- optional `portal` (`admin`, `facilitator`, or `learner`)
-- optional `inviteToken`
-
-This resolves the reported error in `src/app/admin-signin/page.tsx` and also prevents the same error in the facilitator and student sign-in routes.
-
-## Render storage cleanup fix
-
-`src/app/api/admin/accounts/reset/route.ts` imports `deleteStoredFile` and `deleteIdentityFilesOwnedBy`. They are now implemented and exported from `src/lib/render-storage.ts`.
-
-The implementation:
-
-- deletes both the stored file and its JSON metadata sidecar;
-- treats already-missing files as successfully absent, making cleanup idempotent;
-- recursively finds identity-verification metadata;
-- removes identity files only when their stored `ownerEmail` matches an account being deleted;
-- restricts bulk identity cleanup to the `identity-verification` subtree so institutional course materials are not removed accidentally.
-
-## Informational messages
-
-- The npm major-version notice is not a deployment error.
-- `npm audit` vulnerability counts do not cause this build failure by themselves.
-- The Next.js build-cache warning is informational.
-
-## Final v3 correction
-
-The v2 archive still failed TypeScript checking in
-`src/app/api/admin/accounts/reset/route.ts` because that endpoint used
-`db.exec()` for transaction control while `RenderDatabase` exposed only
-`prepare()`.
-
-This package now:
-
-- exposes the underlying SQLite `exec()` operation through `RenderDatabase`;
-- creates the `admin_audit_log` table and index in the runtime schema;
-- includes migration `database/migrations/0012_account_governance.sql`;
-- passes `npm run build` with all 41 application routes generated;
-- passes ESLint with no errors (performance/style warnings only).
-
-## Final v4 staff-portal correction
-
-The former `/fsadmin` route redirected unauthenticated users to
-`/?portal=facilitator`. The public homepage ignores that portal query until a
-session exists, so users appeared to be returned to the same landing page.
-
-This package now:
-
-- serves a working restricted staff gateway at `/fsadmin`;
-- opens facilitator sign-in directly at `/facilitator-signin`;
-- opens system-administrator sign-in directly at `/admin-signin`;
-- removes every staff tab and staff-location link from the normal public
-  landing page;
-- keeps learner access at `/student-signin` and registration at
-  `/student-registration`;
-- sends new facilitator invitations directly to the facilitator extension;
-- binds every authentication request to a portal role, preventing student,
-  facilitator, and administrator credentials from crossing gateways;
-- preserves relative sign-out redirects so Render never exposes
-  `0.0.0.0:10000` to the browser.
-
-The staff URLs are intentionally unadvertised, but they are not treated as the
-security boundary: the API independently verifies the account role before it
-creates a session.
